"""Component layers.0.mlp.down_proj:2823: an ALL-CAPS detector.

It fires on tokens whose letters are all uppercase, such as ERR, FAILED, NAME, PASS,
FIG, or the caps pieces of identifiers and acronyms (.PIPE, GL_TEXTURE, NASA split as
"S" "OUT"). A single capital letter (U, S, A) fires a little weaker than a multi-letter
caps piece. An underscore that directly follows an all-caps piece (GL_, NAME_) also
fires. Ordinary lowercase words, Capitalized words, digits and punctuation stay near 0.

Plain-terms summary: the component says "this piece of text is shouting / is a
constant or acronym", and it carries no information about what comes next.
"""

READS = ()


def _letters(text):
    return [c for c in text if c.isalpha()]


def _is_caps(text):
    letters = _letters(text)
    return len(letters) > 0 and all(c.isupper() for c in letters)


