"""Layer 0, MLP down-projection, component 2833.

A weak feature that mostly reads the current token; it has no clean concept, and this
program captures only its largest, most readable parts. Its activation is:

  * negative on the opening single curly quote ‘ (about -0.3);
  * strongly negative on a form feed, a page break (about -0.7; rare);
  * negative on a line break that follows a space: " \\n" about -0.12, " \\r\\n" about
    -0.06, and only -0.01 for " \\n\\n";
  * slightly positive (about +0.03) on identifier-style symbols common in code and
    markup: underscores, backticks, a literal backslash-n, ~ and ->;
  * slightly negative (about -0.03) on brackets, operators and separators common in code:
    ( ;\\n ();\\n + | ", /* < @.

Every other token is predicted as 0.
"""

