"""A word-level proximal-reference signal, strongest on 'this'.

It recognizes several translations of 'this' and related pointing words.
For English 'this', capitalization and proximity to the document's start
raise the signal; 'like this' and 'do this' attenuate it.
Relative 'which' is weaker after prepositions than after a comma.
