"""Estimate a multilingual response to short s/z-like spelling fragments.

A sigma following Greek letters gets a strong negative estimate; isolated
sigma gets a weaker one. This approximates Greek prose versus mathematical
notation. Other sibilant letters and short Latin fragments have smaller
responses, adjusted for word starts and the preceding letter. Unrecognized
tokens stay near zero. The only state is the preceding token, reset at each
new document; this is a spelling heuristic, not a phonetic transcription.
