capacity phrase, the words that are followed by "of" or "to" or by a counted noun:

* number words two to nine, and "both" / "many" (~0.7; "two years", "both sides");
* totality words all / whole / entire / total / overall / full / percent (~0.3-0.9);
* nouns of lacking and capacity (lack ~2, ability, possibility, chance, role, way(s) ~0.5);
* "of" or "to" right after such a noun ("lack of" ~1.9, "number of" ~0.5);
* a few abstract-noun markers from Vietnamese, Thai and Japanese (sự, việc, ความ, การ, cách),
